  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Primary Path",
      "items": [
        "POST /api/certificates/extract takes {certificate, fileType} and returns {certificateNumber, holderName, certificateName, issuer, issueDate, expiryDate, status}",
        "The Java CLI is a thin client: it Base64-encodes a local file and calls the same endpoint, so extraction happens only on the server",
        "Missing or ambiguous fields stay null — the parser never guesses a value"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Local Processing Only",
      "items": [
        "PDFBox and Tess4J/Tesseract are in-process libraries: no network call leaves the host and no AI or external OCR service is contacted",
        "Scanned PDFs are rendered at 220 DPI and OCR'd for at most 5 pages; PNG/JPG/JPEG images go straight to OCR",
        "OCR needs a native Tesseract runtime on the host (README notes the Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable on Windows)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust Boundary",
      "items": [
        "Untrusted Base64 is validated before parsing: fileType allow-list, non-empty and ≤ 10 MB decoded, magic-byte signature matched to fileType",
        "Failures return a structured error envelope with a code; stack traces, Base64 and certificate text are never returned",
        "The CLI applies the same 10 MB limit locally before uploading"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Marked Unknowns",
      "items": [
        "No authentication or authorization is configured in this repository — the endpoint is open on :8080",
        "Deployment target, TLS termination and runtime hardening are not configured here; the README only documents local `java -jar` runs",
        "There is no persistence layer: extracted fields are returned and discarded, and issuer authenticity or digital signatures are never verified"
      ]
    }
  ]
